.Dd October 16, 2026
.Dt LCC-BLUETOOTH 1
.Os @PROJECT_VERSION@

.Sh NAME
.Nm lcc-bluetooth
.Nd configure Bluetooth devices and settings.

.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h | -help
.Op Fl v | -version

.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is part of the Lumina Control Center.
It enables or disables Bluetooth, controls discoverability and its timeout,
scans for nearby devices, and pairs, connects, disconnects and removes
devices.
Output from the underlying tools is shown in a log pane.
.Pp
.Nm
is a front end and does not talk to the Bluetooth stack directly.
At startup it detects the first available backend, in this order:
.Bl -enum -offset indent
.It
.Xr bluetoothctl 1
(BlueZ, most Linux systems)
.It
.Xr hcitool 1
(older BlueZ)
.It
.Xr hccontrol 8
(FreeBSD)
.El
.Pp
If none is found, the log reports that no Bluetooth management system was
detected.

.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Display help on command line options.
.It Fl v , Fl -version
Display version information.
.El

.Sh DEPENDENCIES
One of the following runtime utilities is required:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Ic bluetoothctl
.It Ic hcitool
.It Ic hccontrol
.El

.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /usr/local/bin/lcc-bluetooth
.It Pa ~/.config/lumina-desktop/lcc-bluetooth.conf
Saved settings for this utility.
.El

.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lcc 1 ,
.Xr bluetoothctl 1

